# What b1nix publishes, and in what pieces.
#
#   name | paths | deps | description
#
# Paths are relative to build/<arch>/rootfs; an absolute path is taken as-is,
# for anything that is not staged there. Missing paths are skipped, so a manifest entry for something this
# build did not produce costs a warning rather than a failure.
#
# The split exists to keep a download small. A machine that wants to run b1nix
# needs the kernel and the base; everything else is a choice. Nothing here
# re-hosts an Alpine package — sway, foot, mesa's userspace and the rest come
# from Alpine's own mirror, which is already faster and better replicated than
# anything we would run.
#
# Sizes are the reason for each line, not an accident of it:
#   the kernel with debug information is 33 MB and without it 5 MB, so the
#   symbols are their own package and nobody downloads them by mistake;
#   the smoke binaries are 439 files nobody runs on a real machine;
#   OSMesa alone is 55 MB, and only a machine doing software GL wants it.

b1nix-kernel      | boot/kernel.elf                                    |             | The b1nix kernel, stripped
b1nix-kernel-dbg  | boot/kernel.elf.debug                              | b1nix-kernel | Debug symbols for the kernel
b1nix-base        | lib/libc.so lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1 sbin/init bin/sh bin/busybox etc/inittab | b1nix-kernel | Minimum userspace to reach a shell
b1nix-drm         | lib/modules                                         | b1nix-kernel | Loadable driver modules
b1nix-tools       | bin/bpkg bin/mountinfo sbin/mountinfo               | b1nix-base  | b1nix's own utilities
b1nix-mesa        | lib/libOSMesa.so.8 lib/libEGL.so.1 lib/libGLESv2.so.2 | b1nix-base | Software OpenGL built for b1nix
b1nix-netsurf     | bin/netsurf-fb                                      | b1nix-base  | NetSurf, framebuffer frontend
b1nix-tests       | bin/m101t_smoke bin/font_probe bin/m51_freetype_smoke | b1nix-base | Smoke and probe binaries
